not good for cancer. I have been taking spirulina and florella which has

00:00:28,990 --> 00:00:35,390
much iron and it constipates me. I learned these are great for breast cancer but is the iron

00:00:35,950 --> 00:00:44,270
produced not worth the health benefits. I could be wrong but I don't think there's a lot of iron

00:00:44,270 --> 00:00:54,830
and florella and spirulina. But certainly iron can be constipating especially if it's

00:00:54,830 --> 00:01:00,750
if it's ferrous sulfate which is a lot of the iron of the market which is just elemental iron

00:01:00,830 --> 00:01:11,950
which is bad. I don't know how much iron is in those things. I don't think there's a lot of iron in

00:01:11,950 --> 00:01:19,950
that. You know, iron that's in food like in different foods. That's a food-based iron that's

00:01:19,950 --> 00:01:30,270
totally different. If you're taking exogenous iron because you have low hemoglobin, low red blood cells,

00:01:30,750 --> 00:01:39,390
if you have an amemia, you want to if your take have to take iron exogenously for your amemia,

00:01:39,390 --> 00:01:46,350
you want to take an iron bisglycinate, a good quality iron that is

00:01:49,070 --> 00:01:56,190
similar to a plant-based iron, double bonded to an amino acid. I always suggest taking

00:01:56,190 --> 00:02:03,790
artimisticid with the iron because if your cancer cells are gobbling out iron, you want them to

00:02:03,790 --> 00:02:10,830
gobble up the artimisticid, the artimisticid travels with iron so it'll then cause the cancer cell

00:02:10,830 --> 00:02:16,430
to gobble up the artimisticid that could help kill the cancer cell. So if you have to take iron

00:02:16,430 --> 00:02:23,390
because of an amemia then I would do that. If you don't have an amemia but you're getting iron

00:02:23,470 --> 00:02:29,870
in just food, then I wouldn't be concerned about that. We could certainly take artimisticid. If you

00:02:29,870 --> 00:02:35,790
think that the chlorella and spirulina has too much iron, you could take its artimisticid with it.

00:02:36,990 --> 00:02:45,950
But I am not an advocate to use iron skillets as a way to get iron. Now, understand, I don't think

00:02:46,750 --> 00:02:52,030
that if you're using a cast iron skillet, you're getting a lot of iron from that skillet

00:02:52,030 --> 00:02:57,950
as long as they don't think you are. If your iron skillet has been properly

00:02:59,070 --> 00:03:07,550
prepared, meaning that it's got a coating on it of fat, which your iron skillet should have

00:03:07,550 --> 00:03:16,030
if you read it correctly. So you're not getting a lot of iron from iron skillets, but some people

00:03:16,030 --> 00:03:25,900
have done that and that can be a issue. I always use a carrier oil, I think you're referring to

00:03:25,900 --> 00:03:32,060
the frankincense. Yeah, then I don't have a perfect answer for you. I don't know if that's a good

